      "text": "personal resources affect individual differences in personality trait development late in life. Personality Trait Development Late in Life The current study contributes to the existing considerations of personality trait development until late in life (Lucas & Donnellan, 2011; Roberts & DelVecchio, 2000; Roberts et al., 2006; Staudinger & Kunzmann, 2005). Our results are in line with conceptual notions and empirical evidence that personality traits change across adulthood and that patterns of change differ across personality traits. Our study extends previous findings by examining personality trait change in very old age and at the very end of life. Corroborating and extending earlier reports (Kandler et al., 2015; Lucas & Donnellan, 2011), we found that mean levels of extraversion and openness are lower at older ages. Thus, our results for these two traits suggest that trends of decline",
